{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"waived-scope-gap","classStatement":"Measure 1 does not define or verify ordinary waived scopes.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"Design lines 61–67 require reporting waived scopes. AC6 and R6 cover only waives after a FAIL streak; neither defines or tests how a waiver without that streak affects the scope or `met`.","failureScenario":"A review scope is waived without a prior FAIL -> the report leaves it open or omits it and gives the wrong convergence result.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"defect-confirmation-gap","classStatement":"Measure 3 does not require confirmation of the escaped defect.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"Design line 74 counts confirmed escaped defects. AC8 requires a qualifying link basis but does not require the escaped defect itself to be confirmed; R8's 'unconfirmed link' check does not resolve that distinction.","failureScenario":"An unconfirmed escaped-defect note has a human-stated link to a demoted finding -> AC8 permits it in the reported defect count.","id":"F2","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"denominator-rubric-gap","classStatement":"The rubric does not verify the required measure denominators.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC11 requires each measure to state its denominator, but R11's pass condition tests missing-field handling only; no rubric row requires denominator evidence.","failureScenario":"A report shows rates without their denominators -> every stated rubric test can pass while AC11 remains unmet.","id":"F3","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"mcp-call-rubric-gap","classStatement":"The rubric verifies MCP tool registration without verifying its behavior.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC12 requires a read-only MCP `convergence` tool, while R12 requires only that tests list the tool.","failureScenario":"The MCP server advertises `convergence` but calls fail or return an i